Subject: [PATCH] driver core: Don't retry deferred probes while probing is blocked

dpm_prepare() and device_shutdown() call device_block_probing(), after
which really_probe() defers every probe.  driver_deferred_probe_trigger()
still queues the deferred probe work in that state, and
deferred_probe_work_func() calls device_pm_move_to_tail() for each device
it retries before bus_probe_device() defers it again.

During a system suspend/resume transition that takes the device, its
children and its consumers off dpm_prepared_list, dpm_suspended_list,
dpm_late_early_list or dpm_noirq_list and puts them back on dpm_list, so
they miss the remaining phases.  Without resume_early, the
pm_runtime_disable() of the late suspend phase is never balanced.  Without
complete, the usage count taken in device_prepare() leaks, RPM_BLOCKED is
never cleared and power.is_prepared stays set.  A device moved during a
suspend phase after its completion was reinitialized is never completed
either, so an asynchronous parent or supplier waiting for it blocks.

The deferred probe timeout makes this easy to hit: it fires
deferred_probe_timeout seconds after the last driver registration, from a
workqueue the freezer does not stop.  On Samsung Galaxy Tab S9 (SM8550)
boards a platform-level suspend test runs at about that time during boot.
When the timeout landed inside it, the LPASS LPI pinctrl, still waiting
for the ADSP, was left with runtime PM disabled.  Every later pin mux
request then failed with -EACCES and the VA macro probed without its DMIC
pins:

  gpio gpiochip9: PM: parent 6e80000.pinctrl should not be sleeping
  va_macro 6d44000.codec: error -EACCES: Error applying setting, reverse things back

Don't retry anything while probing is blocked: leave the pending list
alone in driver_deferred_probe_trigger() and stop the work at the next
device.  defer_all_probes is now written under deferred_probe_mutex, which
both hold when they check it, so no retry can start once
device_block_probing() has returned.  device_unblock_probing() already
triggers a retry of every pending device.

Fixes: 013c074f8642 ("PM / sleep: prohibit devices probing during suspend/hibernation")

--- a/drivers/base/dd.c
+++ b/drivers/base/dd.c
@@ -97,6 +97,17 @@ static void deferred_probe_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 	 */
 	mutex_lock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
 	while (!list_empty(&deferred_probe_active_list)) {
+		/*
+		 * While probing is blocked for a system sleep transition or for
+		 * shutdown, every probe below would be deferred again, and
+		 * device_pm_move_to_tail() would take devices that the PM core
+		 * is suspending or resuming off its lists, so they would miss
+		 * their remaining callbacks.  Leave the rest of the list to the
+		 * retry that device_unblock_probing() triggers.
+		 */
+		if (defer_all_probes)
+			break;
+
 		private = list_first_entry(&deferred_probe_active_list,
 					typeof(*dev->p), deferred_probe);
 		dev = private->device;
@@ -184,6 +195,16 @@ void driver_deferred_probe_trigger(void)
 	 * into the active list so they can be retried by the workqueue
 	 */
 	mutex_lock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
+	/*
+	 * Probing is blocked during system sleep transitions and shutdown, so
+	 * a retry now could only defer every device again.  Keep them on the
+	 * pending list: device_unblock_probing() triggers again once probing
+	 * is allowed.
+	 */
+	if (defer_all_probes) {
+		mutex_unlock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
+		return;
+	}
 	atomic_inc(&deferred_trigger_count);
 	list_splice_tail_init(&deferred_probe_pending_list,
 			      &deferred_probe_active_list);
@@ -203,7 +224,13 @@ void driver_deferred_probe_trigger(void)
  */
 void device_block_probing(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Under deferred_probe_mutex, so that the deferred probe work cannot
+	 * start another retry once this returns.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
 	defer_all_probes = true;
+	mutex_unlock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
 	/* sync with probes to avoid races. */
 	wait_for_device_probe();
 }
@@ -216,7 +243,9 @@ void device_block_probing(void)
  */
 void device_unblock_probing(void)
 {
+	mutex_lock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
 	defer_all_probes = false;
+	mutex_unlock(&deferred_probe_mutex);
 	driver_deferred_probe_trigger();
 }
 
